  "motif": "lamp",
  "intro": "<p>Light is one of the commonest ideas in names anywhere. Latin has <em>lux</em> (Lucy, Lucia, Lucius), Arabic has <em>nur</em> (Noor, Nura, Nuri), Hebrew has <em>or</em> (Ori, Lior, Uriel), and Sanskrit has <em>dipa</em>, 'lamp' (Diya, Kuldeep). This list gathers real names from those families and more, each meaning checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary. Where a name ranks in England and Wales, the ONS figure appears beside it.</p><p>Some of the best-known 'light' names on baby name sites don't hold up. Helen and Eleanor are often said to mean light, and Lucas and Luke are nearly always linked to <em>lux</em>, but the evidence is weaker than the claim. Those are marked uncertain, with the reason.</p>",
